  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Proposed design; not implemented",
      "items": [
        "Source: Agent Core Template Spec at revision b43f461. One FastAPI service on port 8000; modules are not separate microservices.",
        "OpenAI Agents API and Data MCP in remote mode are external integrations; provider sessions retain execution context, while SQLite stores application history.",
        "Mock Data MCP: /mcp/data. Knowledge–Memory MCP: /mcp/knowledge-memory. Keep both MCP routes behind internal ingress."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Message processing",
      "items": [
        "The API validates scope, saves the message and run, and locks the conversation in one transaction. It returns 202 after commit; clients poll results and events.",
        "The worker claims the run and creates or reuses a session through the provider adapter. OpenAI returns pending function calls; the worker delegates MCP access to the bridge.",
        "The worker persists tool results before returning them to the provider. Only root-turn completion finishes a run; response sources must match persisted tool results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Authorization & recovery",
      "items": [
        "The bridge derives scope from the stored AuthContext and signs short-lived credentials. Each MCP validates permissions again; the model cannot choose arbitrary identities, URLs, or tool names.",
        "Each conversation has a separate session and a pinned config revision. An orchestrator is shop configuration, rather than a dedicated container.",
        "Unknown provider outcome → reconciling. Still unknown at the recovery deadline → failed run + blocked conversation. Stream loss alone does not trigger message resubmission."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Limits & modes",
      "items": [
        "180 seconds/run · 15 seconds/MCP call · up to 8 tool calls/run · 4 concurrent runs across the service.",
        "Offline: fake provider + MCP fixtures. Live: real OpenAI + MCP fixtures. Remote Data MCP replaces the mock and does not use its fixtures.",
        "The MVP includes data, knowledge, and history tools. Specialist agents, sandbox execution, vector databases, proactive monitoring, and shop actions belong to later phases."
      ]
    }
  ]
